+## Archive remotes, pdfium, self-updating tools, ffmpeg resources and the ORT ABI guard
+
+**Archive `remote`.** Add `member` (one file) or `dir` (a directory; `"."` is the archive root) to a `remote` entry and
+the pinned archive (`sha256` is always the archive digest, checked before anything else) is extracted instead of copied.
+`format` (`tgz` or `zip`) is inferred from the URL. Optional `memberSha256` pins the extracted member and `executable: true`
+marks it executable. Examples from ScrapeRight:
+
+```js
+{ kind: "remote", name: "agent-browser", url: "https://registry.npmjs.org/agent-browser/-/agent-browser-0.35.1.tgz", sha256: "<tgz>",
+  member: "package/bin/agent-browser-win32-x64.exe", memberSha256: "<exe>", dest: "src-tauri/resources/runtime/agent-browser.exe", platforms: ["win"] },
+{ kind: "remote", name: "yt-dlp", url: "https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/download/<tag>/yt-dlp_win.zip", sha256: "<zip>",
+  dir: ".", dest: "src-tauri/resources/runtime/yt-dlp", clean: true, selfUpdating: true, platforms: ["win"] },   // yt-dlp.exe + _internal/
+{ kind: "remote", name: "deno", url: ".../v2.9.5/deno-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip", sha256: "<zip>", member: "deno.exe", dest: "src-tauri/resources/runtime/deno.exe" },
+```
+
+Guards: every archive entry name is listed first and refused if it is absolute, has a drive letter or backslash, or a `..`
+segment (zip-slip); only the selected member or directory is extracted, into a scratch directory, and the result is refused
+if it contains a symlink, a hard link or a non-regular file (symlink escape). Nothing is cleaned or placed until extraction
+and the member digest pass. A directory remote writes one receipt row per file (`fromDirectory: true`, zero-byte files allowed).
+`deps.extractArchive` replaces the default `tar` (bsdtar) extractor in tests. Errors: `STAGE_SIDECAR_EXTRACT_FAILED`, `_HASH_MISMATCH`.
+
+**`selfUpdating: true`** (per `remote` row, for tools the app replaces at runtime, such as yt-dlp). The `sha256` is still
+required: it pins the INITIAL archive, and the build fails closed on any mismatch. Receipt rows carry `selfUpdating: true` and
+`pinnedInitialSha256: true`, so downstream verifiers know the digest describes the shipped state, not the running state.
+A `/latest/` URL is refused unless `selfUpdating: true` is set; a moving URL still cannot bypass the pin.
+
+**`pdfium`.** `{ kind: "pdfium", version: "chromium/8021", catalog, resourceDir?, as?, licenseDir?, cacheDir? }` works like
+`onnxruntime` against the `pdfium` rows of `native-libraries.json`. A pdfium row may pin the archive alone (`verification.method:
+"archive-sha256"`); a row `sha256` for the library, when present, is verified too. The Windows row `pdfium-chromium-8021-windows-x64`
+is `pinned` (archive `pdfium-win-x64.tgz`, sha256 from ScrapeRight `package.ps1`; the `bin/pdfium.dll` digest is not yet recorded).
+
+**ffmpeg `dest: "resource"`** (with optional `resourceDir`, default `src-tauri/resources/runtime`). The tool is staged as
+`<resourceDir>/<tool>[.exe]`, not an externalBin: the receipt row has `externalBin: false` and `dest: "resource"`, the
+externalBin-named intermediate in `stageDir` is removed, and `externalBinNames` omits it. Universal macOS merges straight into it.
+
+**ONNX Runtime ABI guard.** Before downloading, the `onnxruntime` entry's `version` (major.minor) must equal the ORT API version
+the `ort` crate expects. The crate version comes from `Cargo.lock` (`ort-sys`, else `ort`; looked up at `Cargo.lock` then
+`src-tauri/Cargo.lock`, or `abi.cargoLock`) through a table (`ORT_CRATE_API_VERSIONS`: rc.10 -> 1.22, rc.11 -> 1.23, rc.14 -> 1.24);
+an unlisted crate version fails with `STAGE_SIDECAR_ORT_ABI_UNKNOWN` unless `abi.apiVersion` is set. After staging, the library
+file name (when versioned) and its bytes (ASCII or UTF-16LE) must carry the pinned version string. Mismatch is
+`STAGE_SIDECAR_ORT_ABI_MISMATCH`. The receipt records `ortAbi { crateVersion, apiVersion, stagedVersion }`. No `ort` in the lock
+skips the guard; `abi: false` opts out; `abi: { cargoLock?, apiVersion? }` configures it.
+
+
+## Content digests, DirectML, whisper, Chrome for Testing, unpinned self-updating tools, command pins and the shared cache (round 2)
+
+**ffmpeg compares the content digest, not the whole file (#753, bug fixed).** A catalog row's `contentSha256` is the
+signature-independent digest of `crates/rightkit-ffmpeg/src/content_digest.rs` (a Mach-O without its signature, a PE without its
+certificate table and checksum). `content-digest.mjs` is a byte-for-byte port (`contentIdentity`, `contentDigestFor`); the staged file,
+a local `sources` path and an unpacked archive member are all compared with it, so a correct signed binary no longer fails
+`STAGE_SIDECAR_HASH_MISMATCH`. A malformed Mach-O/PE is `STAGE_SIDECAR_CONTENT_DIGEST_INVALID`, never a whole-file fallback. The
+receipt row keeps `sha256` (the whole file) and adds `contentSha256`.
+
+**onnxruntime DirectML (#724).** For a Windows onnxruntime row that is the DirectML build, the catalog's single approved/pinned
+`directml` row for the same os/arch is staged and hash-checked with it (`DirectML.dll` from its own nupkg, picked by architecture folder),
+with its notices; a missing or ambiguous companion row refuses. Extra files a row lists in `files: [{ artifactFileName, sha256, archiveMember? }]` are staged too.
+
+**`whisper`.** `{ kind: "whisper", version: "1.9.3", ggmlVersion: "0.20.2", from: "../vendor/whisper", catalog, resourceDir?, licenseDir?, aliases?: "major" }`
+stages the `whisper-cpp` row and every `ggml` row of those versions for the target. The catalog holds no download for them, so the
+bytes come from `from` and each file must equal its row (`contentSha256`, else `sha256`) before anything is copied. `aliases: "major"` also
+writes regular copies named like the install names (`libggml.0.dylib`). No universal row exists.
+
+**`chrome-for-testing`.** `{ kind: "chrome-for-testing", version, product?: "chrome" | "chromedriver" | "chrome-headless-shell", sha256: { win64, linux64, "mac-arm64", "mac-x64" }, dest, clean? }`
+downloads `https://storage.googleapis.com/chrome-for-testing-public/<version>/<platform>/<product>-<platform>.zip`, verifies the pinned zip and
+stages the product directory at `dest` (one receipt row per file, `source: "chrome-for-testing"`). The macOS `chrome` app bundle holds
+framework symlinks, which are never extracted; use `chrome-headless-shell`, `chromedriver` or a `command` entry for it.
+
+**`remote.latest`** (needs `selfUpdating: true`, excludes `sha256`): `latest: { checksumsUrl, name? }` reads the digest of the file from the release's own
+`SHA2-256SUMS` (one `<hex>  <name>` line; `name` defaults to the URL's file name), then downloads and verifies against it. The receipt
+marks `unpinned: true`, `resolvedSha256` and `checksumsUrl`. A missing, repeated or conflicting line fails closed.
+
+**`command` outputs.** `sha256` pins a file output (checked before anything is copied). `directory: true` stages a directory output at `dest`
+recursively (one receipt row per file) and `treeSha256` pins the whole tree with the `sha256-tree-v1` digest `sign-dev-artifact` refresh uses.
+
+**Shared download cache.** `RIGHT_RELEASE_DOWNLOAD_CACHE=<absolute dir>`, or `sharedCache: true` in the wrapper form (then
+`%LOCALAPPDATA%\rightkit\downloads`, `~/Library/Caches/rightkit/downloads` or `$XDG_CACHE_HOME`/`~/.cache/rightkit/downloads`), puts the
+content-addressed downloads (`remote`, ffmpeg sources, catalog archives) in one directory shared by every checkout. Entries are named by sha256 and re-hashed on every read.
+
+**Other.** `preflight.stopApps` / `right-release stop-app --dir`, `preflight.commands[].expect`, `legal.cargoNotices` / `license-notices cargo`,
+`legal.binaryNotices` / `license-notices binaries [--receipt]` (every staged remote/command/cmake/prebuilt program needs a declared licence text) and the
+`runtimeArtifacts` block validation are described in the package README and CHANGELOG.
